      {
        "@value": "Physiological strain placed on the body by elevated ambient temperature and humidity, impairing thermoregulation and increasing the risk of heat-related illness."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#inScheme": [
      {
        "@id": "https://vocab.destiny-evidence.org/health-exposure"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@value": "Heat stress (Exposure)"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#scopeNote": [
      {
        "@value": "As the planet warms, heat waves are becoming more frequent and lasting longer — placing people at increased risk for heat-related illnesses such as heat stroke. Heat-related illness can be seen at temperatures much lower than those characteristic of a heat wave. Health impacts: heat-related illness and death.\n"
      }
    ]
  },
