  {
    "@id": "https://vocab.destiny-evidence.org/population-vulnerability",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#ConceptScheme"
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/description": [
      {
        "@value": "Vulnerable population groups relevant to climate and health research, including those with chronic conditions, disabilities, and socioeconomic disadvantages. Vulnerability is the risk of a specific population to be adversely affected. It covers factors affecting susceptibility to harm and lack of capacity to cope and adapt. It describes the social, cultural, economic, and demographic factors that mediate how hazards will manifest as impacts (e.g. gender, education, poverty, disability, age). "
      }
    ],
    "http://purl.org/dc/terms/title": [
